      ":question/id": "d2f7f9de-0d91-5c5a-a9df-0be418285cd3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]$ at $t=-1$ given that $∇f(x,y)=\\left(2 x + 2 y e^{x y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2 x e^{x y} + 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nIn addition, we've been given that\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\left(2 x + 2 y e^{x y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2 x e^{x y} + 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we substitute $x=3 t^{2}$ and $y=t$ into $∇f(x,y)$ to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =\\left(2 x + 2 y e^{x y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2 x e^{x y} + 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\Big|_{x=3 t^{2},\\,y=t} \\\\  & =\\left(2 t \\left(3 t + e^{3 t^{3}}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2 t \\left(3 t e^{3 t^{3}} + 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\left(6 t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(2 t \\left(3 t + e^{3 t^{3}}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2 t \\left(3 t e^{3 t^{3}} + 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\left(6 t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(2 t \\left(3 t + e^{3 t^{3}}\\right)\\right)\\cdot \\left(6 t\\right)+\\left(2 t \\left(3 t e^{3 t^{3}} + 1\\right)\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(36 t^{3} + 12 t^{2} e^{3 t^{3}}\\right)+\\left(6 t^{2} e^{3 t^{3}} + 2 t\\right) \\\\  & =2 t \\left(18 t^{2} + 9 t e^{3 t^{3}} + 1\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the above at $t=-1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]\\Big|_{t=-1} & =2 t \\left(18 t^{2} + 9 t e^{3 t^{3}} + 1\\right)\\Big|_{t=-1} \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{12 \\left(-1 + 3 e^{3}\\right)}{e^{3}}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{2 \\left(-3 + e^{3}\\right)}{e^{3}}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{2 \\left(-9 + 19 e^{3}\\right)}{e^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
